URL:https://jackofthewood.com/events/old-time-jam-4-2026-09-02-2026-09-09-
 2026-09-16-2026-09-23-2026-09-30-2026-10-07-2026-10-14-2026-10-21/
SUMMARY:OLD-TIME JAM
DESCRIPTION:\nThe roots of Appalachian old-time music stretch far across th
 e Atlantic and we're proud to honor and showcase that legacy at Jack of th
 e Wood Pub with our long-running Old-Time Jam sessions — every Wednesda
 y starting at 5pm! Recently recommended by Rolling Stone for "those lookin
 g for an organic\, participatory [music] experience" in Asheville\, the Ol
 d-Time Jam is one of several weekly traditional jam sessions hosted at JAC
 K.\n\n\n\nOur cozy Celtic pub is the perfect spot downtown to take in some
  of the region's finest traditional acoustic musicians playing "in the rou
 nd" while you enjoy a pint or two and the best pub fare in town!\n\n\n\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://jackofthewood.com/wp-content/uploads/202
 5/09/JOTW_WED-OldTimeJam_2025-RollingStoneQuote_IG_1080x1350.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Jack of the Wood
UID:12215@jackofthewood.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261022T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261022T213000
DTSTAMP:20260918T140231Z
URL:https://jackofthewood.com/events/bluegrass-jam-special-edition-featuri
 ng-the-darren-nicholson-band/
SUMMARY:BLUEGRASS JAM SPECIAL EDITION FEATURING THE DARREN NICHOLSON BAND
DESCRIPTION:\nA Grammy nominee and the winner of 13 International Bluegrass
  Music Association awards\, Darren Nicholson has taken his own brand of mo
 untain music around the world. A regular for years on the Grand Ole Opry a
 nd a founding member of acclaimed bluegrass group Balsam Range\, Darren no
 w spends his time recording\, writing new songs\, and performing original 
 roots music inspired by the history &amp\; culture of his native Western N
 orth Carolina — homegrown\, wholehearted music with a purpose.\n\n\n\nA
  punchy mandolinist with instrumentation nods to Bill Monroe and Marty Stu
 art\, Darren is also an introspective songwriter\, technical harmony singe
 r\, convincing lead vocalist\, and a man on a mission. His shows are a tai
 lored experience — genuine\, entertaining\, and an extended handshake to
  the community.\, reflecting the fun-witted and approachable character for
 med in his raising.\n\n\n\nDarren’s passion is sharing raw\, honest-to-g
 oodness\, quality music with his audience. Music that’s good for his sou
 l and theirs too. “That’s all I want\,” says Darren. “I want to be
  a positive part of other people’s lives with music\, you know? I want t
 o be an ambassador to roots music – tip my hat to the past while looking
  forward at the same time. This music was intended to be played in a way t
 hat adds joy to the community. All I want is to restore that purpose\, not
  to complete a transaction.” \n\n\n\nDarren says that when you come out
  to a show\, whatever you do\, please come talk afterward. “I’m like W
 illie Nelson. ‘I don’t want fans\, I want friends.’ It’s a communa
 l thing.” \n\n\n\nYou can catch Darren almost every week sharing the mu
 sic he loves somewhere\, traveling both nationally and internationally —
  as a solo artist\, in collaboration with other musicians\, and with his o
 wn Darren Nicholson Band — a group of Appalachian musicians with a comm
 on respect for and love of American acoustic music who creatively blend bl
 uegrass\, folk\, gospel\, and swing into a new music experience. \n\n\n\n
 Doors at 6pm —&nbsp\;show starts at 7pm. Suggested cover at the door. Op
 en Jam follows at 9:30pm.\n\n\n\n\nhttps://youtu.be/1WLUcPovyCY?si=aywqVKc
 i4-9xcC3C\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://youtu.be/ed8sKWA3CCQ?si=rjF1JGqa7dCv61yW\n\n\
 n\n\n\nhttps://youtu.be/8QlDK2gCsLk?si=ZBXy3C8Y2Hjycp0I\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps:/
 /youtu.be/5oUJ-AP-20U?si=l_R6ciyESeMSgy3N\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://jackofthewood.com/wp-content/uploads/202
 6/08/DarrenNicholsonBand_2026.jpg
END:VEVENT
